Participation Rules
1. Competition Time:
Participants can register during the specified tournament opening period. In the week the tournament begins, Monday to Friday is designated for forming teams. On Friday, team registration starts at 5:00 AM and closes at midnight (24:00), and the official matches begin at 1:00 PM on Saturday;

2. Registration Rules:
Each team must consist of 6 members, and registration can only be completed after all members click “confirm.” Team captains are responsible for submitting the registration;

3. Participation Rules:
①. A maximum of 32 teams can register for the tournament. Qualification will be determined based on the total 6v6 score of all team members. Teams with higher total scores will have priority in obtaining participation slots;
②. Before the official matches commence on Saturday, team members must be online and form their team. Between 12:45-13:00, team captains must click “Start Matching” to confirm participation. Teams that fail to click within the specified 15 minutes will be considered as forfeiting the match. Matching cannot proceed if: any team member is offline、the team includes members who were not registered、or the team has fewer than 3 members;
③. Once the captain clicks “Start Matching,” the team enters the matching process. If the team wins a match, it will automatically stay in matching status without requiring another click. However, if any member in One Dan leaves the team, causing the team to have fewer than 3 members, the matching status will be canceled, and the team will no longer be able to participate in the tournament. It is crucial to ensure that the team has 3 or more members at all times and is consistently in matching status;

Competition Mode
1. After registration ends, teams will be randomly grouped for matches conducted in a single elimination format;
2. If one team fails to match, the opposing team will automatically win the match. If neither team matches, the winner will be chosen randomly;
3. Teams participating in the tournament cannot have duplicate professions. If a team contains members with the same profession, it will be unable to proceed with tournament matching preparations. (The same profession is defined as professions with identical Name values, e.g., Monk and Shura are considered distinct professions);
4. Each tournament round lasts for 15 minutes, but from the semifinals onward, matches will follow a best-of-three format;

Special Situations
1. If server instability or similar circumstances arise after the tournament begins, causing a round to fail to start, the affected match will be postponed to the next scheduled match time. Teams must monitor system announcements and the remaining match preparation time displayed within the game;
2. If any match fails to properly determine a winner, the result for that match will be voided, and the match will automatically be rescheduled 30 minutes later for the next round. Other teams will not need to rematch — the subsequent rounds will simply be delayed;
3. If matches are excessively delayed due to extraordinary reasons and any remaining rounds are scheduled to begin at 11:30 PM or later, these matches will automatically be postponed to the following Saturday at 1:00 PM. Teams should pay attention to system announcements and prepare adequately before the rescheduled matches.

